; The signature the digest regression compiles beside tests/Booleans-rules.eo,
; for what that one cannot reach.
;
; The desugar stage asks the input's semantics for a nil predicate only where
; the nil of an n-ary symbol is not ground, since only then can it not write
; the predicate itself; see Desugar::finalizeDeclaration. str.++ is such a
; symbol -- its nil is the empty sequence of the element type -- so a rule that
; names it is what makes the stage emit the call, and so what makes the driver
; keep the block that answers it, see inline_called_blocks in
; tools/eoc/driver.py. Nothing in tests/Booleans-rules.eo has a nil that is not
; ground, so a run over that signature exercises only the branch that keeps
; nothing.

(include "../../../tests/Strings-theory.eo")

; If two concatenations that start alike are equal, so are their remainders.
(declare-rule str_concat_lprefix ((s String) (t String :list) (u String :list))
    :premises ((= (str.++ s t) (str.++ s u)))
    :conclusion (= t u)
)
